## solution

#### using a vector

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <math.h>

std::string middleValue(Node* head) {
  std::vector<std::string> values;
  Node* current = head;
  while (current != nullptr) {
    values.push_back(current->val);
    current = current->next;
  }
  return values[std::floor(values.size() / 2)];
}
```

- n = number of nodes
- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(n)


#### using two pointers

```cpp
std::string middleValue(Node* head) {
  Node* slow = head;
  Node* fast = head;

  while (fast != nullptr && fast->next != nullptr) {
    fast = fast->next->next;
    slow = slow->next;
  }
  return slow->val;
}
```

- n = number of nodes
- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(1)
